<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Only the pages a signed-out visitor can actually reach and that are worth
  ranking. Everything behind authentication is deliberately absent and is also
  disallowed in robots.txt.

  Every URL here uses the www host. That is the canonical domain - the apex
  redirects to it - and a sitemap listing the non-canonical host just asks
  Google to pick a winner itself.

  Lives in public/ so it is served as a real file rather than being swallowed by
  the SPA rewrite. Dates are the last meaningful content change, not the last
  deploy; bumping them on every deploy teaches Google to stop trusting them.
-->
